<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 3 September, from 36 BCE to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/sextus-pompey" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sextus-pompey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">36 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,061 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Agrippa defeats Sextus Pompey's fleet off Naulochus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Off Naulochus in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, Octavian's admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-vipsanius-agrippa">Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa</a> defeated the fleet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sextus-pompey">Sextus Pompey</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> the Great and last leader of organised opposition to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate">Second Triumvirate</a>. Sextus was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sextus-pompey">Sextus Pompey</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate">Second Triumvirate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">590 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,436 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gregory the Great is consecrated Pope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gregory, a former prefect of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> turned monk, was consecrated pope after months of reluctance. He reorganised the Church's estates, sent missionaries to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and shaped the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">863 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Byzantine forces destroy Umar al-Aqta's army at Lalakaon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Paphlagonia, a Byzantine army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petronas">Petronas</a> encircled and destroyed the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umar-al-aqta">Umar al-Aqta</a>, emir of Melitene, who had sacked Amisos on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>; Umar was killed. The victory began <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>'s offensive on its eastern frontier.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lalakaon">Battle of Lalakaon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1260">1260 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">766 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mamluks defeat the Mongols at Ain Jalut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the spring of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Ain Jalut</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jezreel-valley">Jezreel Valley</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahri-mamluks">Bahri Mamluks</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutuz">Qutuz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> defeated a Mongol army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>. It halted the Mongol advance into Egypt and confirmed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> as the dominant regional power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Battle of Ain Jalut</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1650">1650 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">376 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cromwell routs the Scottish army at Dunbar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Trapped against the coast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell</a> attacked at dawn and shattered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Leslie's larger Scottish army. Dunbar opened the way to the English conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Paris recognises American independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and American envoys signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1783">Treaty of Paris</a>, ending the Revolutionary War and fixing the new nation's borders at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> signed separate treaties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> the same day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France declare war on Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> ignored ultimatums to withdraw from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> declared war. Neville Chamberlain announced it to the nation in a sombre radio broadcast.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy secretly signs an armistice with the Allies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Italian and Allied officers signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-cassibile">Armistice of Cassibile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, the same day British troops landed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>. When it was announced on 8 September, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> occupied much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sweden switches to driving on the right</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At 4.50 am all traffic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> stopped, changed sides and restarted on the right. Dagen H, 'H Day', went remarkably smoothly after years of preparation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 3 September <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eugene-de-beauharnais"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eugene-de-beauharnais.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eugène de Beauharnais</span><span class="tp">1781–1824</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/urho-kekkonen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/urho-kekkonen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Urho Kekkonen</span><span class="tp">1900–1986</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gaston-thorn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gaston-thorn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gaston Thorn</span><span class="tp">1928–2007</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 3 September <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/umar-al-aqta"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Umar al-Aqta</span><span class="tp">d. 863</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gian-galeazzo-visconti"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gian-galeazzo-visconti.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</span><span class="tp">1351–1402</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oliver-cromwell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Oliver Cromwell</span><span class="tp">1599–1658</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adolphe-thiers"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adolphe-thiers.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adolphe Thiers</span><span class="tp">1797–1877</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edvard-benes"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edvard-benes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edvard Beneš</span><span class="tp">1884–1948</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
